{% comment %}
  "Look at the frame" — a material comparison against typical UK retail.

  No competitor is named. Every claim sits at the level of what UK retailers in
  this price band actually publish on their own product pages. The evidence, the
  exact wording rules, and the claims we are NOT entitled to make are recorded in
  docs/price-comparison-evidence.md. Re-verify before every release.

  Brook sits inside the £130-£250 high-street band, so it gets a price row and the
  argument is "same money, better material". Solenne at £749 is dearer than the two
  full-length pieces we could evidence (£425, £569), so it gets NO price row. We do
  not show a favourable number while hiding an unfavourable one; we simply argue on
  material there. See the evidence file before adding one.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign show_comparison = false
  assign our_glass = ''
  assign their_bands = ''

  case product.handle
    when 'brook-champagne-gold-wall-mirror', 'brook-matte-black-wall-mirror'
      assign show_comparison = true
      assign our_glass = '4 mm, copper-free and lead-free'
      comment
        One band per size variant, in variant order. A single band would quote the
        small-mirror band next to the large mirror's price. Sources in the evidence file:
        73x52 -> La Redoute £120.99, G&G £129, M&S £139, Oliver Bonas £160, G&G £165, John Lewis £250
        90x65 -> Oliver Bonas £195, Atkin & Thyme £219, John Lewis £250, Cox & Cox £425
      endcomment
      assign their_bands = '£130 to £250|£195 to £425'
    when 'solenne-champagne-gold-full-length-mirror'
      assign show_comparison = true
      assign our_glass = '5 mm, copper-free and lead-free'
  endcase

  assign checked_on = '10 July 2026'
-%}

{%- if show_comparison -%}
<section class="honesty" aria-labelledby="honesty-title">
  <div class="container honesty-grid">

    <div class="honesty-copy">
      <span class="honesty-eyebrow">Priced with honesty</span>
      <h2 class="honesty-title" id="honesty-title">Turn the mirror over.<br><em>That is where the money went.</em></h2>

      <p class="honesty-lede">
        An asymmetrical mirror looks much the same in a photograph whatever it is made of.
        The difference is in the frame you never see, and it is the reason one mirror is
        still perfect in a steamy bathroom in ten years and another is not.
      </p>

      <p class="honesty-body">
        We went through the asymmetrical mirrors that UK homeware and high-street shops sell
        between £120 and £400. They are framed in iron, in wood, in MDF, or in metal that is
        never specified. We could not find a single mainstream UK retailer selling one framed
        in stainless steel. Not one published a copper-free or lead-free glass claim. Not one
        offered a multi-year warranty.
      </p>

      <ul class="honesty-points">
        <li>
          <strong>304-grade stainless steel.</strong>
          The grade used in professional kitchens. It does not rust, tarnish or corrode
          indoors. Iron does, once the paint is chipped.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Copper-free, lead-free glass.</strong>
          The silvering is applied without the copper and lead used in conventional mirror
          production. Cleaner to make, and it will not creep black at the edges.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A five-year warranty.</strong>
          Against frame corrosion, joint failure and delamination. We offer it because the
          materials let us.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="honesty-panel">
      <table class="honesty-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"><span class="honesty-vh">Comparison</span></th>
            <th scope="col" class="honesty-us">MUNLER</th>
            <th scope="col">Typical UK retail</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Frame</th>
            <td class="honesty-us"><strong>304 stainless steel</strong></td>
            <td>Iron, wood or MDF</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Glass</th>
            <td class="honesty-us"><strong>{{ our_glass }}</strong></td>
            <td>Not stated</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Warranty</th>
            <td class="honesty-us"><strong>5 years</strong></td>
            <td>Not stated</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">UK delivery</th>
            <td class="honesty-us"><strong>Free, insured, tracked</strong></td>
            <td>Often charged</td>
          </tr>
          {%- if their_bands != blank -%}
            {%- assign band_list = their_bands | split: '|' -%}
            {%- assign size_idx = 0 -%}
            {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
              {%- assign vt = variant.title | downcase -%}
              {%- unless vt == 'default title' -%}
                {%- assign band = band_list[size_idx] -%}
                {%- if band -%}
                  {%- assign size_label = variant.title | split: ' - ' | first -%}
                  <tr class="honesty-row--price">
                    <th scope="row">{{ size_label }}</th>
                    <td class="honesty-us"><strong class="honesty-price">{{ variant.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</strong></td>
                    <td><span class="honesty-price honesty-price--them">{{ band }}</span></td>
                  </tr>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- assign size_idx = size_idx | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      {%- if their_bands != blank -%}
      <p class="honesty-kicker">Same money. Better mirror.</p>
      {%- else -%}
      <p class="honesty-kicker">Built to outlast the room it hangs in.</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <p class="honesty-foot">
        Based on the asymmetrical wall mirrors listed by UK homeware and high-street retailers
        between £120 and £400, and the frame materials they publish on their own product pages,
        checked on {{ checked_on }}. We name no one: iron and wood are honest materials, they
        are simply not the same materials.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}
